        453.8751220703125,
        151.46771240234375
      ],
      "text": "In our rather futuristic society for a number of reasons people are getting more interested in the\npast of their hometowns. With the help of rapidly ameliorating technology their desire to learn\nabout the history can be easily put into life. But what are the roots of such an eagerness?\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        33.69199752807617,
        155.04852294921875,
        455.58758544921875,
        257.7711181640625
      ],
      "text": "First of all, the hectic lifestyle that we all experience nowadays does not leave any space for\ncalmness and peace in our souls, s0 most of the people - especially adolescence - are struggling\nwith finding their feet, whilst having a broad spectrum of Knowledge about the world around really\ngives a feeling of confidence in the impermanence of life. In addition to this, it is said that being\naware of the past you can change the future. Consequently, if people want to live a better life in\nmore comfortable environment, they have to explore the history of their homes in order not to\nrepeat past mistakes.\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        32.383487701416016,
        265.610595703125,
        461.1875305175781,
        368.00738525390625
      ],
      "text": "For this aims we are lucky to have multiple tools to carry out research into the subject. Despite\nlibraries being considered as an old-fashioned and not necessarily convinient approach of learning,\nthere are actually quite a few books and magazines which are not available online but which are\nextremely helpful when it comes to the local interests. News, photos, articles and interviews with\ndifferent people published in old magazines indeed provide with a clear image of past events.\nBrousing the internet forums is also a great idea to find new information and make friend with\nmutual objectives.\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        31.40216827392578,
        376.82684326171875,
        452.9117431640625,
        392.8710632324219
      ],
      "text": "Putting everything into a nutshell, learning about the history of your place not only builds a sense\n"
    },
